{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And the beginning of his kingdom was Bavel.</b> This is to inform us that during the days of his kingdom it came about — when the nations came to the land of Shinar — that the city and the tower were devised, in order that his rule might extend over the entire human species through the mediation of a universal foreign deity for the whole species, unto whom nations would inquire, after the manner of Jeroboam's counsel, as he feared inquiry at the Temple (1 Kings 12:26)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "Sforno's אֵל נֵכָר (\"foreign god/deity\") is rendered literally; the sense is a deity other than YHWH serving as a universal object of worship for all humanity."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:29:45.187257476Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}